<div class="fr-panel" data-panel="quality">
  <p class="fr-panel-note">The structural quality question for this group is not how fast AUM grows but how durable the fee stream is. We proxy durability with the share of fee-paying AUM that is perpetual or permanent capital, and plot it against the multiple the market is paying on fee-related earnings.</p>
  <div class="fr-callout"><strong>Why this matters.</strong> A high EV/FRE multiple is only expensive if the underlying fee stream is episodic. Names in the upper-right — high perpetual capital, high multiple — are paying up for durability, which is defensible. Names in the lower-right — high multiple, low perpetual capital — carry the most re-rating risk. The lower-left is where value-trap candidates cluster: cheap, but cheap because the earnings are realisation-dependent.</div>
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title">Perpetual-Capital % (x) vs EV/FRE Multiple (y) — bubble size = fee-paying AUM</div>
    <div id="fr-scatter"></div>
    <div class="card-foot">Perpetual / permanent capital includes insurance-linked, non-traded perpetual vehicles and other locked structures as % of fee-paying AUM. Illustrative.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="tbl-wrap" style="margin-top:16px;"><table id="fr-quality-tbl"></table></div>
</div>

<div class="fr-panel" data-panel="insurance">
  <p class="fr-panel-note">The defining structural shift in the group is the migration of insurance and spread balance sheets onto alt-AM platforms. Permanent insurance liabilities fund credit origination, converting episodic fundraising into a perpetual spread-earnings engine. This is increasingly the whole bull case for APO and KKR.</p>
  <div class="fr-callout"><strong>The spread engine.</strong> Spread-related earnings (SRE) are far more annuity-like than carry, and they scale with general-account assets. APO/Athene is the mature template; KKR/Global Atlantic is scaling into it; ARES/Aspida is the small-base, fastest-growth optionality the market has not fully priced. BX runs the asset-light variant — it manages insurance assets without owning the liabilities, capturing fees but not spread.</div>
  <div class="tbl-wrap"><table id="fr-ins-tbl"></table></div>
  <div class="grid2" style="margin-top:16px;">
