<div class="fr-panel" data-panel="earnings">
  <p class="fr-panel-note">Earnings quality across the group hinges on two things: the mix of fee-related vs market-dependent earnings, and the degree to which stock-based compensation is inflating reported margins. Both are management-defined adjustments and reward scrutiny.</p>
  <div class="fr-callout"><strong>SBC creep.</strong> Stock comp is typically excluded from FRE and DE by management, which flatters reported margins relative to GAAP. The cleaner comparable is SBC-adjusted FRE margin. Where SBC runs high as a share of after-tax earnings, reported margins overstate true economics — ARES carries the highest ratio in the group and the trend bears watching.</div>
  <div class="grid2">
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-title">Earnings Mix: FRE / SRE / PII ($B LTM)</div>
      <div id="fr-mix-chart"></div>
